  "findings": "NATIVE_PUBLIC38_ADEQUATE subject=sha256:ab24edb57620292039baec0e56f0122a37e64b44134271c07bc333879bde4011 product=04b83a5f394431e1dcca533889f6c02e32d02a0d evidence_sha256=d82597bc05e88e3d029f0c13f24f1c2e08afea3b6e70eebeee907da441c0db10\n\nBoth original native lanes completed 38 operations, including 19 phase queries, with 37 process captures and 65 artifacts per lane. Readback covered seven ENV4 observations and eight PUBLIC6 phases, with 19 PASS, zero NONPASS and zero GAP assertions per lane. Both lanes recorded the exact operational refusal with exit 1, empty stdout and UnexpectedOutcome, followed by final reader exit 0.\n\nThe graph and historical Ed25519 verification records agree on the controller, lane manifests, original attempts, grants, journals and result bytes. The pinned OpenSSL checks supply the signature verification omitted by the raw readers. The six-role DTO preserves both original signature-only GAP records through their pins and records the combined PASS separately. The whole-script controls reject the supplied nonpositive signature and divergent manifest before emitting PASS files.\n\nThe current freeze builder resolves both prior findings. It compares the pinned event stream's completed findings with the exact DTO-bound acceptance line and requires a positive source verdict and original-host flag on each lane. It cross-checks manifest, attempt and result-byte bindings, commits the review and DTO in one direction, and checks both destinations for vacancy before either write. The whole-finalize controls reject the prior rejected audit under a favorable wrapper and reject missing or negative source verdicts, a false host flag, and nonpositive readbacks. The synthetic positive reaches both simulated write batches with identical common candidate-freeze bytes.\n\nI relied on the supplied machine-checked hashes and reviewed the packet without tools or file edits. The mock created no freeze B. Private evaluation follows the exact B commitments and the custodian checks. This verdict covers public observations and freeze preparation under the stated trust boundary and grants zero R0 credit or authority.",
